($wh$wh2021:19:1316$wh$,$wh$usda.wood-handbook.2021$wh$,1316,19,$wh$Specialty Treatments$wh$,$wh$19–15$wh$,481,$wh$Heebink, B.G.; Haskell, H.H. 1962. Effect of heat and humidity on the properties of high-pressure laminates. Forest Products Journal. 12(11): 542–548. Hill, C.A.S. 2006. Wood modification: chemical, thermal and other processes. Chitchester, West Sussex, UK: John Wiley and Sons, Ltd. Rowell, R.M., ed. 1984. The chemistry of solid wood. Advances in Chemistry Series No. 207. Washington, DC: American Chemical Society. Rowell, R.M., ed. 2012. Handbook of wood chemistry and wood composites, 2nd edition. Boca Raton, FL: CRC Press. 703 p. Hoadley, R.B. 1980. Understanding wood: a craftsman’s guide to wood technology. Newtown, CT: The Taunton Press. Rowell, R.M.; Lange, S.; McSweeny, J.; Davis, M. 2002. Modification of wood fiber using steam. In: Proceedings, 6th Pacific Rim Bio-Based Composites Symposium. Portland, OR. Hurst, K. 1962. Plywood bending. Australian Timber Journal. (June.) Schneider, M. 1994. Wood polymer composites. Wood and Fiber Science. 26(1): 142–151. Inoue, M.; Norimoto, M.; Tanahashi, M.; Rowell, R.M. 1993. Steam and heat fixation of compressed wood. Wood and Fiber Science. 25(3): 224–235. Schneider, M.; Witt, A.E. 2004. History of wood polymer composites commercialization. Forest Products Journal. 54(4): 19–24. Jorgensen, R.N. 1965. Furniture wood bending, part I. Furniture design and manufacturing. (December.) Schuerch, C. 1964. Principles and potential of wood plasticization. Forest Products Journal. 14(9): 377–381. Jorgensen, R.N. 1966. Furniture wood bending, part II. Furniture design and manufacturing. (January.) Seborg, R.M.; Inverarity, R.B. 1962. Preservation of old, waterlogged wood by treatment with polyethylene glycol. Science. 136(3516): 649–650.$wh$),
